        <mxCell id="p3_n1" value="1" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#202124;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="75" width="26" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_n2" value="2" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#202124;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="250" width="26" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_n3" value="3" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#202124;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="340" width="26" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_n4" value="4" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#202124;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="530" width="26" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_n5" value="5" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#202124;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="615" width="26" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_n6" value="6" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#202124;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="810" width="26" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_n7" value="7" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#202124;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="915" width="26" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p3_why" value="WHY AN AI ORCHESTRATOR? (the brain)&#10;&#10;It decides: which model · whether RAG is needed · whether SQL is&#10;required · whether an agent/tool runs · which prompt template ·&#10;how conversation context is managed.&#10;&#10;Without it every request hits the LLM directly → higher cost,&#10;slower answers, no grounding, no auditability.&#10;&#10;Here: LangGraph graph with conditional edges; state is typed&#10;(graph/state.py) and checkpointed per session." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1210" y="60" width="480" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_res" value="RESILIENCE PATTERNS (all with live examples)&#10;&#10;• Fallback chain — provider failover ollama→claude→gpt→gemini (LIVE ai/registry)&#10;• Degrade gracefully — LLM down → deterministic keyword router still routes (LIVE)&#10;• Timeout guard — semantic search capped at 2.5s so a slow embed never stalls chat (LIVE)&#10;• Checkpointer degradation — graph runs stateless if checkpoint DB unavailable (LIVE)&#10;• Retry w/ backoff — WS reconnect 1s→2s→4s→…30s + offline send-queue (LIVE frontend)&#10;• Self-correction — NL2SQL retries once with the error attached (LIVE)&#10;• Circuit breaker + bulkhead per provider — PLANNED&#10;&#10;Interview line: &quot;every dependency has a timeout, a fallback, or both.&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1210" y="275" width="480" height="230" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_mod" value="INPUT MODALITIES&#10;text — LIVE · voice — LIVE in classic PA (Web Speech API STT + TTS) · image — PLANNED (vision-capable model via gateway)&#10;&#10;PROMPT SERVICE (prompts-as-code)&#10;Versioned AgentPrompt objects in core/prompt_registry.py — review like code, A/B per version, instant rollback. Real example: nl2sql_generator v1 → v2 (added SQLite-dialect rules) after a live failure." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1210" y="520" width="480" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_ten" value="MULTI-TENANCY &amp; ISOLATION&#10;Live pattern: Qdrant category-as-tenant partitioning (is_tenant=True → per-tenant HNSW subgraphs, filtered ANN only touches that slice). Enterprise scale-out: per-tenant collections/schemas, per-tenant quotas + rate limits, row-level security in SQL.&#10;&#10;REALTIME vs BATCH&#10;Realtime: streaming chat (WS). Batch: scheduled morning briefing + nightly consolidation (APScheduler/Celery — LIVE in classic PA). Batch inference = cheaper, cacheable, off-peak.&#10;&#10;SSE vs WEBSOCKET&#10;WS chosen: bidirectional (ping, cancel, client sends mid-stream), one connection for chat+events. SSE fine for pure one-way token streams behind proxies." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1210" y="705" width="480" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_leg" value="LEGEND — green solid = LIVE (file path shown) · amber dashed = PLANNED · numbered = request order 1-7 · yellow labels on edges = route decision" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1210" y="960" width="480" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p3_batch" value="Scheduled / batch lane (LIVE in classic PA): APScheduler 07:00 morning briefing · 22:00 nightly consolidation · Celery workers — same LLM service, off-peak" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="906" width="240" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_e28" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#00897b;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p3_batch" target="p3_llm"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

  <diagram id="p4" name="4 · Request Flow &amp; Intent Routing">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1060" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="p4_t" value="REQUEST FLOW &amp; INTENT ROUTING — not every prompt should go to the LLM directly. Routing improves accuracy AND cost: grounded routes hallucinate less, and cheap deterministic paths skip expensive models." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p4_chat" value="Chat message arrives" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="140" y="60" width="220" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_int" value="INTENT DETECTION&#10;one LLM call → {route, plan, reason} · keyword fallback" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="120" y="140" width="260" height="54" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_q1" value="Document question?" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="250" width="170" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_q2" value="Database / analytics?" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="330" width="170" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_q3" value="Action / API call?" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="410" width="170" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_q4" value="Multi-step workflow?" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="490" width="170" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_q5" value="Fresh web info?" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="570" width="170" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_q6" value="General chat / writing?" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="650" width="170" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_r1" value="→ RAG (grounded, citations)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="250" width="210" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_r2" value="→ NL2SQL (guarded SELECT)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="330" width="210" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_r3" value="→ Function Calling (validated tool)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="410" width="210" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_r4" value="→ Agent (multi-step tool loop)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="490" width="210" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_r5" value="→ Web Search (URL citations)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="570" width="210" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_r6" value="→ LLM direct (memory/secretary)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="290" y="650" width="210" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_chat" target="p4_int"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_int" target="p4_q1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_q1" target="p4_q2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_q2" target="p4_q3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e5" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_q3" target="p4_q4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e6" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_q4" target="p4_q5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e7" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_q5" target="p4_q6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e8" value="yes" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_q1" target="p4_r1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e9" value="yes" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_q2" target="p4_r2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e10" value="yes" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_q3" target="p4_r3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e11" value="yes" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_q4" target="p4_r4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e12" value="yes" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_q5" target="p4_r5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e13" value="default" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_q6" target="p4_r6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p4_ex" value="ROUTING EXAMPLES (memorize these pairs)&#10;&#10;&quot;Show me yesterday&#39;s sales&quot;…………………→ NL2SQL&#10;&quot;Explain the leave policy&quot;……………………→ RAG&#10;&quot;Book an appointment&quot;………………………→ Agent / tool&#10;&quot;Write an email to the vendor&quot;……………→ LLM direct&#10;&quot;Analyze this uploaded PDF&quot;………………→ RAG + LLM&#10;&quot;Generate Python code&quot;………………………→ LLM (code model)&#10;&quot;Latest RBI circular on KYC?&quot;………………→ Web Search&#10;&quot;Remind me to call John at 3pm&quot;…………→ Memory agent&#10;&#10;Live examples from this build (verified E2E):&#10;&quot;How many notes this month?&quot; → nl2sql → COUNT over pa_entries → &quot;1 note&quot;&#10;&quot;Latest stable Python version&quot; → web_search → 6 URL citations" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="560" y="60" width="480" height="290" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_json" value="THE SUPERVISOR CONTRACT (live JSON)&#10;&#10;{&#10;  &quot;route&quot;: &quot;nl2sql&quot;,&#10;  &quot;plan&quot;: [&quot;count meetings this month&quot;,&#10;              &quot;lookup contract notice period&quot;],&#10;  &quot;reason&quot;: &quot;analytics over own data + doc lookup&quot;&#10;}&#10;&#10;• Temperature 0 · parsed with regex fallback&#10;• Invalid route → deterministic keyword router&#10;   (unit-tested, works with the LLM fully down)&#10;• route + reason surface in the UI as a badge —&#10;   users see WHY the answer came from where it did" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="560" y="370" width="480" height="270" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p4_mq" value="MULTI-INTENT: &quot;Show all claims approved yesterday AND summarize the fraud policy&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1130" y="60" width="540" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_mi" value="Intent Detection → plan[] with 2 parts (LIVE: planner emits plan[])" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1180" y="140" width="440" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_p1" value="Part 1 → NL2SQL&#10;claims approved yesterday (SELECT w/ date filter)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1130" y="220" width="255" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_p2" value="Part 2 → RAG&#10;fraud policy summary w/ [Policy.pdf · p.N] citations" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1415" y="220" width="255" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_comb" value="Combine Results&#10;PLANNED — LangGraph Send API parallel fan-out + merge node with source attribution; today the dominant route wins" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fef7e0;strokeColor=#d79b00;dashed=1;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1180" y="310" width="440" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_fin" value="LLM generates final answer&#10;&quot;12 claims were approved yesterday [SQL]. The fraud policy requires… [Policy.pdf · p.4]&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1180" y="400" width="440" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e14" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_mq" target="p4_mi"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e15" value="part 1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_mi" target="p4_p1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e16" value="part 2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_mi" target="p4_p2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e17" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_p1" target="p4_comb"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e18" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_p2" target="p4_comb"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4_e19" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4_comb" target="p4_fin"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p4_why" value="WHY ROUTING WINS (say this in the interview)&#10;&#10;Accuracy: grounded routes (RAG/SQL) answer from data, not from model &quot;memory&quot; → hallucination drops.&#10;Cost: &quot;hi&quot; should never burn a 175B-parameter model — deterministic/small-model paths are ~free.&#10;Latency: SQL COUNT beats generating a long answer; small models stream faster.&#10;Auditability: each route logs exactly what it retrieved / executed — provable answers.&#10;Safety: actions only via validated tool calls, never free-form model output." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1130" y="490" width="540" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

  <diagram id="p5" name="5 · Memory Architecture">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1000" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="p5_t" value="MEMORY ARCHITECTURE — memory is more than chat history. Five types, each with its own store and lifecycle; all five are implemented (or partially) in this build." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p5_fail" value="WITHOUT MEMORY (the interview opener)&#10;&#10;User: Hi&#10;Bot:  Hello&#10;User: My name is John&#10;Bot:  OK&#10;User: What&#39;s my name?&#10;Bot:  &quot;I don&#39;t know.&quot;  ✗&#10;&#10;LLMs are stateless — every request starts from zero.&#10;Memory is an APPLICATION-layer responsibility,&#10;not a model feature." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fce8e6;strokeColor=#c5221f;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="60" width="330" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p5_m1" value="1 · SHORT-TERM (working) MEMORY&#10;Current conversation context fed into every prompt.&#10;LIVE: session history (pa_conversations, last 12 turns) + LangGraph checkpointed messages channel (thread_id = session_id, survives restarts)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="410" y="60" width="420" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p5_m2" value="2 · LONG-TERM MEMORY&#10;User preferences + durable facts across sessions.&#10;LIVE: pa_entries store notes/tasks/meetings forever; PA_USER_NAME etc. in config. Preference examples: language=EN, timezone=IST, favorite dashboard=Sales" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="410" y="152" width="420" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p5_m3" value="3 · SEMANTIC MEMORY (facts)&#10;Facts extracted from conversations, retrievable by MEANING.&#10;LIVE: every saved entry is embedded (nomic-embed 768-dim) into Qdrant pa_memories; semantic_search(top_k=3, min_score=0.70) injects relevant past context into the prompt" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="410" y="244" width="420" height="82" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p5_m4" value="4 · EPISODIC MEMORY (past interactions)&#10;What happened, when — timeline of past tasks/interactions.&#10;LIVE: pa_entries carry entry_date/hour/week/month; daily briefing + weekly insights are episodic summaries generated from them" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="410" y="342" width="420" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p5_m5" value="5 · VECTOR MEMORY (retrieval by embedding)&#10;The mechanism behind semantic memory + RAG: cosine ANN over embeddings.&#10;LIVE: Qdrant collections pa_memories · doc_chunks · code_chunks — one embedding space per store, all nomic-embed" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="410" y="434" width="420" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p5_tiers" value="STORAGE TIERS (match store to lifetime + access pattern)&#10;&#10;Hot / active session………Redis (pub-sub live here; session cache at scale)&#10;Durable structured…………SQLite → PostgreSQL at scale&#10;   (pa_conversations · pa_entries · pa_reminders · feedback)&#10;Semantic / similarity………Qdrant (768-dim, cosine, int8 quantization)&#10;Graph state…………………AsyncSqliteSaver checkpoint DB&#10;&#10;One brain, two assistants: classic /assistant and /assistant-pro&#10;write to the SAME tables — a reminder set in one fires in both." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="870" y="60" width="420" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p5_ctx" value="CONTEXT-WINDOW MANAGEMENT (what to do when history &gt; window)&#10;&#10;1. Sliding window — keep last N turns (LIVE: history limit 12)&#10;2. Token-budget truncation — LIVE: ai/context_manager.truncate_messages&#10;    reserves output tokens, trims oldest first&#10;3. Summarize-then-drop — replace old turns with an LLM summary&#10;    (LIVE pattern: nightly consolidation compresses the day)&#10;4. Retrieve-instead-of-carry — don&#39;t keep everything in context;&#10;    embed it and semantically retrieve only what&#39;s relevant (LIVE)&#10;&#10;Interview: &quot;context is a budget — spend it on retrieval, not history.&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="870" y="320" width="420" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p5_flow" value="WITH MEMORY — the same dialogue works&#10;&#10;&quot;My name is John&quot; → extracted as a fact → pa_entries + embedded to Qdrant&#10;&quot;What&#39;s my name?&quot; → semantic_search hits [memory] &quot;name is John&quot; (score 0.83)&#10;→ injected into system prompt → &quot;Your name is John.&quot; ✓&#10;&#10;Write path: fire-and-forget embedding (never blocks the reply — LIVE)&#10;Read path: 2.5s timeout guard (slow embed never stalls chat — LIVE)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="330" width="330" height="230" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p5_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p5_m1" target="p5_m2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p5_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p5_m2" target="p5_m3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p5_e3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p5_m3" target="p5_m4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p5_e4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p5_m4" target="p5_m5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

  <diagram id="p6" name="6 · RAG Pipeline Deep-Dive">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1240" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="p6_t" value="RAG PIPELINE DEEP-DIVE — grounding the model in trusted documents to reduce hallucination. Left lane = ingestion (offline). Middle lane = query (per request). Right = the selection decisions interviewers probe." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p6_lane1" value="INGESTION LANE (offline)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#00897b;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="50" width="260" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_i1" value="Document upload&#10;PDF · DOCX · XLSX · audio · video · URL" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="80" width="260" height="50" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_i2" value="Extract&#10;PyMuPDF text · pdfplumber tables · EasyOCR scans · whisper transcripts · trafilatura web" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="160" width="260" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_i3" value="Chunk (locator-aware)&#10;agents/doc_chat/chunker.py — every chunk keeps its citation anchor (file · p.N / Sheet / mm:ss)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="252" width="260" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_i4" value="Embed&#10;nomic-embed-text 768-dim via Ollama, batched" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="344" width="260" height="50" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_i5" value="Upsert → Qdrant doc_chunks&#10;category = tenant partition (HNSW m=0 + payload_m=16 → per-category subgraphs) · int8 quantization · on-disk vectors" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="424" width="260" height="76" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_ie1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#00897b;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p6_i1" target="p6_i2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_ie2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#00897b;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p6_i2" target="p6_i3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_ie3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#00897b;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p6_i3" target="p6_i4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_ie4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#00897b;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p6_i4" target="p6_i5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p6_lane2" value="QUERY LANE (per request)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1a73e8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="50" width="260" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_q1" value="Question&#10;&quot;What does my contract say about the notice period?&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="80" width="260" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_q2" value="Query embedding&#10;same model as ingestion (must match!)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="160" width="260" height="50" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_q3" value="Category routing (metadata filter)&#10;embedding-centroid classifier picks best category subgraph — filtered ANN only traverses that slice" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="240" width="260" height="66" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_q4" value="Vector search → Top-k (6)&#10;cosine ANN; assistant-pro searches ALL collections" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="336" width="260" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_q5" value="Reranking&#10;PLANNED — cross-encoder (bge-reranker) reorders top-50 → best 6; biggest precision win per $ in RAG" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fef7e0;strokeColor=#d79b00;dashed=1;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="418" width="260" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_q6" value="Context + citations&#10;build_context() → [marker] blocks + citation chips, deduped, token-budgeted" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="510" width="260" height="58" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_q7" value="Grounded synthesis (LLM)&#10;&quot;use ONLY excerpts, cite every fact, never invent citations&quot; — streamed" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="598" width="260" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_q8" value="Answer with citations&#10;&quot;60-day notice period [Contract.pdf · p.4]&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="684" width="260" height="50" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_qe1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#1a73e8;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p6_q1" target="p6_q2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_qe2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#1a73e8;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p6_q2" target="p6_q3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_qe3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#1a73e8;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p6_q3" target="p6_q4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_qe4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#1a73e8;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p6_q4" target="p6_q5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_qe5" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#1a73e8;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p6_q5" target="p6_q6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_qe6" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#1a73e8;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p6_q6" target="p6_q7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_qe7" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#1a73e8;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p6_q7" target="p6_q8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_xe" value="index feeds retrieval" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p6_i5" target="p6_q4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p6_chunkp" value="CHUNKING STRATEGIES&#10;&#10;• Fixed-size + overlap — simple baseline (start here)&#10;• Structure-aware — split on headings/pages/sheets (used here:&#10;   locator-aware chunks keep citation anchors)&#10;• Semantic chunking — split at topic shifts (embedding distance)&#10;• Parent-child — retrieve small child chunks, expand to parent&#10;   for context (PLANNED)&#10;Rule: chunk ≈ 200–500 tokens; too big = diluted vectors,&#10;too small = lost context." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="700" y="60" width="480" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_hall" value="HALLUCINATION REDUCTION (layered)&#10;&#10;1. Grounding rule in the prompt: use ONLY excerpts (LIVE)&#10;2. Mandatory citations tied to real retrieved chunks (LIVE)&#10;3. Honesty fallback: &quot;not in your documents&quot; + clearly-labeled&#10;    general-knowledge section (LIVE)&#10;4. Low temperature on grounded routes (0.3) (LIVE)&#10;5. Faithfulness eval (RAGAS) as regression gate (PLANNED)&#10;6. Critic agent verifies citations exist before reply (PLANNED)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="700" y="280" width="480" height="190" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_adv" value="ADVANCED RAG (name-drop with one-line definitions)&#10;&#10;Hybrid search — dense + sparse/BM25 fused (PLANNED; astro corpus designed for it)&#10;Metadata filtering — category/tenant/date filters (LIVE — category routing)&#10;Context compression — drop irrelevant sentences before the LLM (token budget LIVE)&#10;Parent-child retrieval — child finds, parent provides context (PLANNED)&#10;Graph RAG — entity graph traversal for multi-hop questions (PLANNED)&#10;Agentic RAG — agent re-queries / reformulates on low confidence (PLANNED)&#10;Adaptive RAG — router decides no-retrieval / one-shot / iterative per query (partially LIVE: supervisor decides rag vs direct)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="700" y="490" width="480" height="220" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p6_vdb" value="VECTOR DB SELECTION (chosen: Qdrant)&#10;&#10;Qdrant ✓ — local/self-host, tenant partitioning, int8 quantization,&#10;   payload filters, hybrid-ready → fits local-first + multi-tenant&#10;pgvector — simplest ops if you already run Postgres; SQL joins&#10;   with metadata; weaker at very large scale / advanced filtering&#10;Pinecone — fully managed SaaS, zero ops; data leaves boundary, $&#10;Vertex AI Vector Search — GCP-native, huge scale; lock-in&#10;&#10;Criteria: data locality · scale · filtering · hybrid support ·&#10;ops burden · cost · ecosystem" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1200" y="60" width="490" height="220" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_emb" value="EMBEDDING MODEL SELECTION (chosen: nomic-embed-text 768-dim)&#10;&#10;nomic-embed ✓ — local via Ollama, $0, privacy, good quality/size&#10;bge-m3 — stronger multilingual + built-in sparse for hybrid (upgrade path,&#10;   1024-dim — requires re-index!)&#10;OpenAI / Gemini embeddings — top quality, but every document&#10;   leaves the machine + per-call cost&#10;&#10;Rules: ingestion + query MUST use the same model · changing&#10;model = full re-index · dimension × vectors × 4B = RAM budget" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1200" y="300" width="490" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6_kb" value="KNOWLEDGE-BASE LIFECYCLE + RAG EVALUATION&#10;&#10;Lifecycle: upload → index → UPDATE (re-chunk + re-embed changed docs&#10;only, delta by content hash) → curate (review distilled facts) → delete&#10;(vector points + rows — right-to-erasure/GDPR: delete by doc_id filter, LIVE API)&#10;&#10;RAG eval hooks (RAGAS): faithfulness (answer ⊆ context?) · answer&#10;relevancy · context precision (retrieved chunks actually needed?) ·&#10;context recall (did we retrieve everything needed?) — run on the&#10;golden dataset per release; scores are trend metrics with a local judge" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1200" y="520" width="490" height="210" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

  <diagram id="p7" name="7 · NL2SQL Pipeline Deep-Dive">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1060" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="p7_t" value="NL2SQL PIPELINE DEEP-DIVE — natural language → guarded SQL → read-only execution → narrated answer. FULLY LIVE in this build, including the self-correction loop. The security layers are the interview differentiator." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p7_s1" value="Question&#10;&quot;How many notes did I write this month?&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="60" width="300" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_s2" value="Schema Retrieval (schema injection)&#10;agents/nl2sql/schema.py — SQLAlchemy inspect() → cached DDL of WHITELISTED tables only (pa_entries, pa_reminders, leads, tasks…). Internal tables invisible to the model." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="138" width="300" height="82" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_s3" value="Prompt (versioned v2)&#10;nl2sql_generator: SQLite dialect ONLY (strftime, never EXTRACT/ILIKE/NOW), table guide, fenced sql output, mandatory LIMIT — v2 added after a live llama3.2 failure" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="250" width="300" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_s4" value="LLM generates SQL&#10;temperature 0.1 via provider registry" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="360" width="300" height="48" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_s5" value="VALIDATION — 5-layer defense&#10;see panel → sqlglot parse · AST walk · whitelist · LIMIT cap · read-only engine" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="438" width="300" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_s6" value="Execution (read-only)&#10;separate engine file:…?mode=ro — writes impossible · 5s timeout · rows capped 200" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="528" width="300" height="58" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_s7" value="Success?" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="140" y="616" width="180" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_s8" value="Result narration&#10;nl2sql_answer prompt: 1-3 sentences grounded ONLY in returned rows + markdown table, streamed" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="686" width="300" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_s9" value="Answer + SQL citation&#10;&quot;You wrote 1 note this month&quot; + the executed SQL shown as a citation chip (transparency)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="778" width="300" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p7_s1" target="p7_s2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p7_s2" target="p7_s3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_e3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p7_s3" target="p7_s4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_e4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p7_s4" target="p7_s5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_e5" value="valid" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p7_s5" target="p7_s6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_e6" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p7_s6" target="p7_s7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_e7" value="error → retry ONCE with error attached" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#c62828;fontColor=#c62828;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p7_s7" target="p7_s4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="440" y="520"/><mxPoint x="440" y="384"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_e8" value="rows ok" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p7_s7" target="p7_s8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_e9" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#7e57c2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p7_s8" target="p7_s9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p7_def" value="THE 5-LAYER SQL-INJECTION DEFENSE (agents/nl2sql/executor.py — all LIVE)&#10;&#10;Layer 1 · sqlglot parse — must be exactly ONE statement and it must be a SELECT&#10;   (CTEs allowed). &quot;SELECT …; DELETE …&quot; → rejected before touching the DB.&#10;Layer 2 · AST walk — Insert/Update/Delete/Drop/Create/Alter/Pragma/Attach/&#10;   Command anywhere in the tree → rejected.&#10;Layer 3 · Table whitelist — every referenced table must be in ALLOWED_TABLES;&#10;   token_usage, users, internal tables → &quot;table not allowed&quot;.&#10;Layer 4 · LIMIT cap — missing LIMIT injected, oversized LIMIT reduced to 200.&#10;Layer 5 · Read-only engine — sqlite ?mode=ro connection: even a validator&#10;   bypass physically cannot write. + 5s asyncio timeout.&#10;&#10;Tested: DELETE, UPDATE, INSERT, DROP, PRAGMA, multi-statement injection,&#10;non-whitelisted tables, prose-not-SQL — 38-test suite, all rejected. ✓&#10;&#10;Interview add-on: at enterprise scale add per-USER row-level permissions&#10;(RLS) so generated SQL can only see that user&#39;s rows." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fce8e6;strokeColor=#c5221f;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="560" y="60" width="540" height="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_live" value="LIVE SELF-CORRECTION EXAMPLE (real trace from this build)&#10;&#10;Attempt 1: llama3.2 generated&#10;  SELECT COUNT(notes) FROM leads WHERE EXTRACT(MONTH …)&#10;  → SQLite has no EXTRACT → execution error&#10;Fix fed back → prompt v2 adds dialect rules → Attempt 2:&#10;  SELECT COUNT(id) FROM pa_entries&#10;  WHERE type=&#39;note&#39; AND strftime(&#39;%Y-%m&#39;, entry_date)=&#39;2026-07&#39;&#10;  → 1 row → &quot;You wrote 1 note this month.&quot; ✓&#10;&#10;Two lessons to tell interviewers:&#10;1. Small local models need explicit dialect constraints in the prompt.&#10;2. One self-correction round fixes most failures; more rounds =&#10;    latency with diminishing returns." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="560" y="410" width="540" height="280" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_eval" value="NL2SQL EVALUATION METRICS&#10;&#10;• SQL execution success rate (target &gt; 97%) — did it run?&#10;• Result accuracy — right answer vs golden query results&#10;• Exact-match / semantic-match of generated SQL (secondary —&#10;   different SQL can be equally correct)&#10;• Guardrail rejection correctness — injections blocked,&#10;   legit queries passed (deterministic tests, LIVE)&#10;• Self-correction recovery rate — % fixed on retry&#10;• Latency: generation + execution &lt; 3s P95&#10;&#10;Benchmark on YOUR schema and YOUR question styles —&#10;public Spider/BIRD scores don&#39;t transfer to your DB." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1130" y="60" width="560" height="250" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p7_perm" value="PERMISSIONS &amp; GOVERNANCE CALLOUT&#10;&#10;&quot;Always validate generated SQL and enforce user permissions&#10;before execution.&quot;&#10;&#10;• The LLM&#39;s SQL runs with the APP&#39;s least-privileged read-only&#10;   role — never a superuser connection&#10;• Whitelist &gt; blacklist: allow known tables, don&#39;t enumerate bad ones&#10;• Log every generated SQL + who asked (audit trail — LIVE via&#10;   tool_calls record + correlation IDs)&#10;• Show the SQL to the user (transparency builds trust — LIVE&#10;   citation chip)&#10;• PII columns: mask or exclude from the whitelist entirely" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1130" y="330" width="560" height="250" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

  <diagram id="p8" name="8 · Agents, Function Calling &amp; Frameworks">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="p8_t" value="AGENTS, FUNCTION CALLING &amp; FRAMEWORKS — the LLM never executes actions itself; it REQUESTS tools, the application validates and executes. Framework choice is a when-to-use question, not a fashion question." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p8_f1" value="User: &quot;Schedule a meeting tomorrow at 10&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="60" width="330" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_f2" value="LLM returns a TOOL REQUEST (not an action)&#10;{ &quot;tool&quot;: &quot;create_calendar_event&quot;,&#10;  &quot;date&quot;: &quot;2026-07-23&quot;, &quot;time&quot;: &quot;10:00&quot; }" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="130" width="330" height="66" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_f3" value="Backend VALIDATES the request&#10;schema check · allowlist · permissions · path-traversal guard (LIVE in tool_dispatcher)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="226" width="330" height="58" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_f4" value="API executes → result&#10;calendar API → event created (ticket / booking / query result)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="314" width="330" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_f5" value="Result returned TO the LLM&#10;ToolResultMessage appended to history — model sees what happened" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="396" width="330" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_f6" value="LLM responds to the user&#10;&quot;Done — meeting booked tomorrow 10:00.&quot; (or requests the NEXT tool → loop)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="478" width="330" height="52" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_fe1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p8_f1" target="p8_f2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_fe2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p8_f2" target="p8_f3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_fe3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p8_f3" target="p8_f4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_fe4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p8_f4" target="p8_f5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_fe5" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p8_f5" target="p8_f6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_fe6" value="agent loop: repeat until text-only reply (max 25 iterations — LIVE)" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#c62828;fontColor=#c62828;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p8_f6" target="p8_f2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="440" y="330"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p8_loop" value="THE REAL AGENT LOOP (core/agent_loop.py — LIVE)&#10;&#10;stream LLM → accumulate tool calls → dispatch ALL calls in&#10;PARALLEL (asyncio.gather) → append results → call LLM again →&#10;repeat until text-only answer (max 25 iterations).&#10;&#10;~25 tools: code search/index, extraction, content generation,&#10;PA notes, web scrape, MCP tools. Token usage recorded per run.&#10;&#10;AGENT TAXONOMY&#10;Workflow agent — fixed steps, deterministic (extraction pipeline)&#10;Autonomous agent — LLM decides next action each turn (this loop)&#10;Planning — decompose before acting (supervisor plan[] — LIVE)&#10;Reflection / self-correction — critique own output and retry&#10;   (LIVE example: NL2SQL error-feedback retry)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="580" width="480" height="290" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p8_fw" value="AGENT FRAMEWORK COMPARISON — WHEN TO USE WHICH&#10;&#10;LangGraph ✓ (used here) — stateful graphs, conditional edges, checkpointing,&#10;   human-in-loop interrupts. Pick for: production control-flow, auditable routing,&#10;   supervisor architectures. (Python/JS, LangChain ecosystem)&#10;CrewAI — role-based &quot;crews&quot; (researcher/writer/reviewer) with tasks &amp; delegation.&#10;   Pick for: quick multi-role pipelines, content workflows. Less low-level control.&#10;Google ADK — GCP-native agent kit (Gemini-first, Vertex integration, eval built-in).&#10;   Pick for: Google-cloud shops wanting managed deployment.&#10;AutoGen (Microsoft) — conversational multi-agent (agents chat with each other),&#10;   group-chat orchestration. Pick for: research/experiments, code-gen duos.&#10;Semantic Kernel — .NET-first, enterprise Microsoft stack, planners + plugins.&#10;   Pick for: existing C#/.NET orgs, M365 integration.&#10;OpenAI Agents SDK — lightweight, OpenAI-native handoffs/guardrails.&#10;   Pick for: OpenAI-only stacks wanting minimal deps.&#10;&#10;Rule: the framework is 10% of the work — eval, guardrails and ops are the 90%." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="580" y="60" width="560" height="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_proto" value="PROTOCOLS — know the difference cold&#10;&#10;MCP (Model Context Protocol) — agent ↔ TOOLS/DATA interop.&#10;Standardizes how a model host discovers and calls tools&#10;(tools/list, tools/call over JSON-RPC).&#10;LIVE HERE: backend/app/mcp/server.py on :6789, protocol&#10;2024-11-05 — this platform&#39;s 25 tools are MCP-exposed.&#10;&#10;A2A (Agent-to-Agent) — agent ↔ AGENT interop. Standardizes&#10;task delegation between independent agents (task lifecycle,&#10;capability cards, artifacts) — including across vendors.&#10;&#10;One-liner: &quot;MCP plugs tools into an agent; A2A plugs agents&#10;into each other.&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1160" y="60" width="530" height="270" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_json" value="STRUCTURED OUTPUT / JSON RELIABILITY&#10;&#10;Why it matters: one invalid JSON breaks the automation chain —&#10;target &gt; 99% validity.&#10;&#10;Techniques (in order of strength):&#10;1. Constrained decoding / native JSON mode (grammar-enforced)&#10;2. Schema validation at the API layer + retry-on-invalid&#10;3. Parse-with-fallback — LIVE: PAAgent._parse tries json.loads,&#10;    then regex-extracts the first {...} block, then degrades to&#10;    plain-text message (never crashes the turn)&#10;4. Low temperature for structured tasks (0.0-0.2)&#10;&#10;Same discipline for tool calls: validate arguments against the&#10;tool&#39;s JSON schema BEFORE executing (function-calling contract)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1160" y="350" width="530" height="290" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p8_multi" value="MULTI-AGENT PATTERNS (see Page 9 for the sequence diagram)&#10;&#10;Supervisor/Coordinator — routes tasks to workers (LIVE: graph/supervisor.py)&#10;Workers — specialists owning one capability + data source (LIVE: 5 nodes)&#10;Planner — decomposes before delegation (LIVE partial: plan[] emitted)&#10;Critic / Reviewer — verifies claims/citations before reply (PLANNED)&#10;Parallel fan-out + conflict resolution — merge worker outputs, prefer&#10;sourced claims, surface disagreements (PLANNED — LangGraph Send API)&#10;&#10;Context sharing tiers: turn-scoped graph state → session checkpoints →&#10;long-term shared DB/vector memory (all LIVE)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="580" y="410" width="560" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

  <diagram id="p9" name="9 · Multi-Agent Sequence (worked example)">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1150" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="p9_t" value="MULTI-AGENT SEQUENCE — Insurance Claim AI worked example: &quot;Was claim #123 approved, and what does the policy say about flood damage?&quot; Read top→bottom; numbers = message order. Same pattern powers support, travel, healthcare, banking agents." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p9_l1" value="User" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_l2" value="API Gateway&#10;+ Auth" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fef7e0;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="240" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_l3" value="Orchestrator&#10;(LangGraph)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="420" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_l4" value="Planner +&#10;Supervisor" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="600" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_l5" value="Worker:&#10;NL2SQL" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="780" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_l6" value="Worker:&#10;RAG" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="960" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_l7" value="Critic&#10;(PLANNED)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fef7e0;strokeColor=#d79b00;dashed=1;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1140" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_l8" value="LLM&#10;Synthesis" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1320" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p9_ll1" style="endArrow=none;dashed=1;strokeColor=#9e9e9e;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="120" y="100" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="120" y="1000" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_ll2" style="endArrow=none;dashed=1;strokeColor=#9e9e9e;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="300" y="100" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="300" y="1000" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_ll3" style="endArrow=none;dashed=1;strokeColor=#9e9e9e;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="480" y="100" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="480" y="1000" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_ll4" style="endArrow=none;dashed=1;strokeColor=#9e9e9e;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="660" y="100" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="660" y="1000" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_ll5" style="endArrow=none;dashed=1;strokeColor=#9e9e9e;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="840" y="100" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="840" y="1000" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_ll6" style="endArrow=none;dashed=1;strokeColor=#9e9e9e;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1020" y="100" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="1020" y="1000" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_ll7" style="endArrow=none;dashed=1;strokeColor=#9e9e9e;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1200" y="100" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="1200" y="1000" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_ll8" style="endArrow=none;dashed=1;strokeColor=#9e9e9e;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1380" y="100" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="1380" y="1000" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p9_m1" value="1 · question (claim #123 status + flood-damage clause)" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="120" y="150" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="300" y="150" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_m2" value="2 · authenticated request + session_id (JWT — planned)" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="300" y="210" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="480" y="210" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_m3" value="3 · plan the turn (load checkpointed state, thread_id=session)" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="480" y="270" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="660" y="270" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_m4" value="4 · {plan:[part1 SQL, part2 RAG], route, reason} — one LLM call" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="660" y="330" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="480" y="330" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_m5" value="5 · delegate part 1: claim #123 status" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="660" y="390" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="840" y="390" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_m6" value="6 · delegate part 2: flood-damage clause (PARALLEL with 5 — planned; sequential today)" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="660" y="450" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="1020" y="450" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_m7" value="7 · SELECT status FROM claims WHERE id=123 (5-layer guarded) → &quot;APPROVED, 2026-07-21&quot; → shared state" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="840" y="530" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="480" y="530" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_m8" value="8 · vector search policy docs → excerpts + [Policy.pdf · p.12] citations → shared state" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1020" y="600" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="480" y="600" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_m9" value="9 · verify: citations exist? SQL matches question? no invented claims? (PLANNED)" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="480" y="670" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="1200" y="670" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_m10" value="10 · verified context → synthesize one answer (conflict rule: sourced claims win)" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1200" y="740" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="1380" y="740" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_m11" value="11 · streamed final answer: &quot;Claim #123 was APPROVED on 21 Jul [SQL]. Flood damage is covered up to ₹5L with 48-hr notification [Policy.pdf · p.12].&quot; + route badges + 👍/👎" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#7e57c2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1380" y="820" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="120" y="820" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_m12" value="12 · persist: conversation + message_id → feedback loop · trace w/ correlation ID" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="480" y="880" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="480" y="940" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p9_notes" value="EXECUTION SEMANTICS&#10;&#10;Sequential (today): supervisor picks ONE worker per turn — simple, auditable.&#10;Parallel (planned): Send API fans out plan parts; barrier before combine.&#10;Inside the tool worker, tool CALLS already run parallel (asyncio.gather — LIVE).&#10;&#10;Context sharing: workers never talk to each other directly — they read/write&#10;the SHARED typed state (blackboard pattern). Long-term context via shared&#10;DB + vector memory.&#10;&#10;Conflict resolution (planned combine node): sourced &gt; unsourced ·&#10;fresher data wins · disagreements surfaced, never averaged away." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1470" y="120" width="230" height="340" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p9_map" value="SAME PATTERN, OTHER DOMAINS&#10;&#10;Customer Support — SQL: order status · RAG: return policy · Tool: create ticket&#10;Travel Agent — Tool: search flights + book · RAG: visa rules · SQL: loyalty points&#10;Healthcare — SQL: appointment slots · RAG: care guidelines · Critic: MANDATORY (safety)&#10;Banking — SQL: balance/txns · RAG: product T&amp;C · Tool: block card · strict RBAC + audit&#10;&#10;In regulated domains the Critic/HITL step is not optional." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1470" y="480" width="230" height="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

  <diagram id="p10" name="10 · Model Selection &amp; Benchmarking">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1240" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="p10_t" value="LLM SELECTION &amp; BENCHMARKING — never start with the model; start with the business problem. There is no universal winner: the weighted scorecard turns opinion into a defensible decision." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p10_s1" value="Business Problem" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="70" y="60" width="200" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_s2" value="AI Requirements" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="70" y="128" width="200" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_s3" value="Evaluation Criteria" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="70" y="196" width="200" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_s4" value="Candidate Models (4-5, never 20)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="70" y="264" width="200" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_s5" value="Benchmark (own data!)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="70" y="332" width="200" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_s6" value="Pilot (per-route overrides)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="70" y="400" width="200" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_s7" value="Production (+ re-benchmark loop)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="70" y="468" width="200" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p10_s1" target="p10_s2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p10_s2" target="p10_s3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_e3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p10_s3" target="p10_s4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_e4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p10_s4" target="p10_s5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_e5" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p10_s5" target="p10_s6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_e6" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p10_s6" target="p10_s7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_e7" value="new models appear" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p10_s7" target="p10_s5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="30" y="420"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p10_req" value="REQUIREMENT MATRIX (importance)&#10;&#10;Accuracy……………High    Reasoning………High&#10;Cost…………………High    Latency…………High&#10;Context window…High    Tool calling……High&#10;Safety………………High    Privacy…………High (local!)&#10;Images………………Med     Voice……………Med&#10;Coding………………Med     Multilingual…Med&#10;&#10;This build&#39;s hard constraints: on-device (Apple GPU),&#10;$0 marginal cost default, JSON-stable, tool-capable" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="70" y="560" width="330" height="230" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p10_bench" value="11 BENCHMARK CATEGORIES (managers compare everything, not just accuracy)&#10;&#10;1  Accuracy — 1000 own-domain questions → 947 correct = 94.7%&#10;2  Reasoning — multi-step logic (&quot;John &gt; Mike &gt; Alex — who&#39;s oldest?&quot;)&#10;3  Hallucination — nonexistent &quot;Policy ABC&quot; → good model says &quot;I don&#39;t know&quot;&#10;4  Context window — can it hold the 300-page PDF + conversation?&#10;5  Latency — P50 / P95 / P99; 300ms feels instant, 8s kills UX&#10;6  Cost — $/M tokens × your volume = business decision (50M tokens/day!)&#10;7  Tool calling — reliable structured {&quot;tool&quot;: &quot;bookFlight&quot;, &quot;date&quot;: &quot;Friday&quot;}&#10;8  JSON reliability — always-valid JSON (one failure breaks the API chain)&#10;9  Multilingual — EN · HI · TA · AR · FR · DE for global users&#10;10 Safety — prompt injection, jailbreak, PII leakage, toxicity, bias, refusal quality&#10;11 Enterprise security — trains on your data? isolation? private deploy? audit? compliance?" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="430" y="60" width="600" height="290" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_data" value="BENCHMARK DATASET — company data, never random internet questions&#10;&#10;Example composition (insurance-flavored):&#10;200 RAG questions · 150 SQL questions · 100 tool calls · 100 summaries ·&#10;100 emails · 100 coding · 100 reasoning · 50 math · 50 images · 50 voice&#10;(≈ 1000 items reflecting REAL usage: 500 claims, 200 underwriting cases,&#10;300 FAQs, 100 policy docs, 50 SQL queries, 20 agent workflows)&#10;&#10;This build&#39;s seed (LIVE): thumbs-down rows exported from assistant_feedback&#10;become the hardest golden items — the dataset grows from real failures." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="430" y="370" width="600" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_res" value="EXAMPLE BENCHMARK RESULTS (illustrative — no universal winner)&#10;&#10;Metric          GPT        Gemini     Claude     Llama (local)&#10;Accuracy        96         95         97         91&#10;Reasoning       96         95         98         90&#10;Cost            High       Low        High       LOWEST ($0 local)&#10;Latency         Medium     Fast       Medium     Fast (on-device)&#10;Context         Large      V.Large    Large      Medium&#10;Tool calling    Excellent  Excellent  V.Good     Good&#10;Enterprise      Excellent  Excellent  Excellent  Depends on deploy&#10;Privacy         Cloud      Cloud      Cloud      TOTAL (on-device)&#10;&#10;→ &quot;best&quot; depends on requirements: this build weights privacy + cost&#10;→ local llama3.2 default, cloud failover for the quality ceiling" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="430" y="590" width="600" height="270" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p10_score" value="WEIGHTED DECISION SCORECARD (transparent, data-driven)&#10;&#10;Criteria    Weight   GPT   Gemini   Claude   Local-Llama&#10;Accuracy     25%      9      9        10        7&#10;Cost         20%      6      9         6       10&#10;Latency      15%      8      9         8        9&#10;Reasoning    20%      9      9        10        7&#10;Security/&#10;Privacy      20%      9      9         9       10&#10;─────────────────────────────────────────────&#10;Weighted     100%    8.3    9.0       8.7      8.6&#10;&#10;Decision here: hybrid — local default (privacy 10, cost 10)&#10;+ cloud failover for hard queries. The scorecard defends&#10;the decision to leadership without opinions." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="60" width="630" height="290" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_kpi" value="KPI TARGETS TO PRESENT TO LEADERSHIP&#10;&#10;Accuracy…………………&gt; 95%        Hallucination………&lt; 2%&#10;Tool success……………&gt; 98%        SQL success…………&gt; 97%&#10;JSON validity…………&gt; 99%        Latency P95…………&lt; 2 sec&#10;Cost/request…………&lt; $0.02       User satisfaction…&gt; 4.6/5&#10;&#10;Report these WEEKLY during pilot, per model AND per route." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="370" width="630" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10_ans" value="THE &quot;AI MANAGER ANSWER&quot; (memorize this structure)&#10;&#10;&quot;We didn&#39;t choose the model on popularity. We shortlisted GPT, Gemini,&#10;Claude and Llama against our functional and non-functional requirements.&#10;We built an evaluation dataset from OUR use-cases — RAG queries, SQL&#10;generation, tool calling, summarization, multilingual tasks — and measured&#10;accuracy, reasoning, hallucination rate, latency, cost, context window,&#10;structured-output reliability and enterprise security. X delivered the best&#10;balance of cost, latency, long-context and integration with our environment,&#10;so it went to production — and our eval harness re-runs on every new model&#10;release, so the decision stays current.&quot;&#10;&#10;For THIS build the honest version: &quot;privacy and $0 marginal cost weighted&#10;highest → local llama3.2 default with per-route overrides (3B fp16 for RAG,&#10;14B for deep synthesis) and cloud failover — all swappable via one config.&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="560" width="630" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

  <diagram id="p11" name="11 · Evaluation, LLM-as-Judge &amp; Observability">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1160" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="p11_t" value="EVALUATION, LLM-AS-JUDGE &amp; OBSERVABILITY — &quot;this is where most candidates struggle.&quot; Evaluate every layer: prompt, LLM output, retrieval, SQL, agents, end-to-end. Offline before release, online in production, continuously forever." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p11_f1" value="Prompt (versioned)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="60" width="220" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11_f2" value="LLM response (per route)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="128" width="220" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11_f3" value="EVALUATION ENGINE&#10;faithfulness · answer quality · context precision/recall · SQL accuracy · tool success · hallucination · latency · cost" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="196" width="260" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11_f4" value="Scores dashboard&#10;per model · per prompt version · per route · trend over releases" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="306" width="220" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11_f5" value="Gate: ship / iterate / rollback" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fce8e6;strokeColor=#c5221f;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="392" width="220" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11_fe1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p11_f1" target="p11_f2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11_fe2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p11_f2" target="p11_f3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11_fe3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p11_f3" target="p11_f4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11_fe4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p11_f4" target="p11_f5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p11_modes" value="EVALUATION MODES&#10;&#10;Offline — golden dataset per release&#10;   (regression gate; deterministic tests&#10;   LIVE: 38 pytest — guardrails, routing,&#10;   structure)&#10;Online — sample live traffic, score&#10;   asynchronously, alert on drops&#10;Continuous — every 👍/👎 + drift signal&#10;   feeds the dataset (loop LIVE via&#10;   assistant_feedback)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="470" width="260" height="230" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p11_fw" value="FRAMEWORK ROSTER — WHEN TO USE WHICH&#10;&#10;RAG + agent quality:  RAGAS (faithfulness, answer relevancy, context precision/recall) ·&#10;   DeepEval (GEval rubric scoring, tool-use assertions, pytest-style)&#10;Tracing / LLM observability:  LangFuse (self-hostable — fits local-first, planned here) ·&#10;   LangSmith (LangChain-native SaaS) · Arize Phoenix (OSS, embedding-drift views) ·&#10;   Opik (Comet, OSS) · Helicone (proxy-based cost/latency analytics)&#10;Prompt testing:  Promptfoo (CI prompt matrix, red-teaming) · OpenAI Evals (registry format)&#10;Feedback functions:  TruLens (groundedness feedback on chains)&#10;Experiment tracking:  MLflow · Weights &amp; Biases (params/metrics/artifacts at scale)&#10;Cloud-native suites:  Vertex AI Evaluation (GCP) · Azure AI Evaluation (Microsoft)&#10;&#10;Picking rule: one TRACING tool + one QUALITY framework + CI tests is enough to start.&#10;This build: pytest (live) → + RAGAS/DeepEval → + LangFuse self-hosted (planned)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="350" y="60" width="640" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11_judge" value="LLM-AS-JUDGE — powerful, but know its failure modes&#10;&#10;Modes: pairwise (A vs B, most reliable) · reference-based (vs golden answer) ·&#10;reference-free (rubric only — weakest, use for trends)&#10;&#10;Judge biases to name in interviews:&#10;• Position bias — prefers the first answer → swap order and average&#10;• Verbosity bias — longer looks better → length-penalize the rubric&#10;• Self-preference — models favor their own outputs → judge ≠ candidate family&#10;&#10;Calibration: validate judge vs ~100 human-labeled items; report agreement&#10;(target κ &gt; 0.7) before trusting it as a gate.&#10;&#10;Local-judge caveat (this build): a 3B judge is noisy → treat scores as TREND&#10;metrics, not hard gates; use a larger judge (cloud or 14B) for release gates.&#10;Human-in-the-loop remains the gold standard for high-risk answers." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="350" y="380" width="640" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p11_metrics" value="METRICS GLOSSARY (three eras — know all three)&#10;&#10;CLASSIC NLP/ML:&#10;Accuracy · Precision (of flagged, how many right) · Recall (of true, how&#10;many found) · F1 (harmonic mean) · BLEU (n-gram overlap, translation) ·&#10;ROUGE (recall overlap, summarization) · BERTScore (embedding similarity)&#10;→ still asked in interviews; weak for open-ended generation&#10;&#10;LLM-ERA QUALITY:&#10;Faithfulness (answer ⊆ retrieved context?) · Groundedness · Answer&#10;relevancy · Context precision (retrieved = needed?) · Context recall&#10;(needed = retrieved?) · Hallucination rate · JSON validity&#10;&#10;OPERATIONAL:&#10;Latency P50/P95/P99 · token usage &amp; cost/request (LIVE: token_usage&#10;table) · tool success · SQL execution success · agent task completion ·&#10;routing accuracy (LIVE: labeled routing tests) · CSAT / 👍-ratio (LIVE)&#10;&#10;BUSINESS: deflection rate · time saved · adoption · revenue impact" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1020" y="60" width="670" height="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11_log" value="LOG &amp; TRACE EVERY INTERACTION (fields)&#10;&#10;user_id · session_id · correlation_id (LIVE — one ID from gateway→&#10;supervisor→node→persist, grep-able) · prompt + prompt_version ·&#10;retrieved doc ids + scores · generated SQL · tool calls + results ·&#10;model + provider · response · latency per stage · tokens in/out ·&#10;cost · route + reason · errors · feedback rating&#10;&#10;LIVE: structlog JSON events; message_id links every reply to its&#10;feedback row. PLANNED: LangFuse trace tree per turn." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1020" y="410" width="670" height="210" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11_loop" value="HUMAN FEEDBACK LOOP (LIVE end-to-end)&#10;&#10;👍/👎 per reply → POST /api/assistant-pro/feedback → assistant_feedback&#10;table {message_id, route, query, response, rating, comment} →&#10;GET /feedback exports → thumbs-down rows become golden-dataset items&#10;→ re-benchmark → prompt/model fix → redeploy. The wheel turns weekly." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1020" y="640" width="670" height="130" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

  <diagram id="p12" name="12 · Deployment, Security, HA/DR &amp; LLMOps">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1300" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="p12_t" value="PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT, SECURITY, HA/DR &amp; LLMOPS — what separates a demo from a product. Every panel is an interview section; LIVE items are from this build, the rest is the hardening roadmap." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p12_stack" value="PRODUCTION STACK (this build → enterprise mapping)&#10;&#10;Frontend………………React/Vite SPA (LIVE) → React/Next.js&#10;Backend…………………FastAPI + WS (LIVE) → FastAPI / Spring Boot&#10;Orchestrator…………LangGraph (LIVE) → LangGraph / Google ADK&#10;DB………………………SQLite (LIVE) → PostgreSQL / AlloyDB&#10;Vector DB……………Qdrant (LIVE) → Qdrant / pgvector / Vertex&#10;Cache/queue…………Redis + Celery (LIVE)&#10;LLM………………………Ollama llama3.2 + cloud failover (LIVE)&#10;   → Gemini/GPT/Claude enterprise endpoints&#10;Containers……………docker-compose partial (LIVE: redis/qdrant/&#10;   searxng) → Docker → Kubernetes / Cloud Run&#10;Metrics…………………→ Prometheus + Grafana&#10;LLM observability…→ LangFuse (self-hosted) / Phoenix&#10;CI/CD……………………→ GitHub Actions (tests LIVE, pipeline planned)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="60" width="400" height="310" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p12_roll" value="ROLLOUT STRATEGIES — when to use which&#10;&#10;Canary — 5% → 25% → 100% of sessions on the new model/prompt;&#10;   watch KPI deltas. DEFAULT for LLM changes.&#10;Blue/Green — two full stacks, instant switch + instant rollback.&#10;   Use for risky infra changes.&#10;Shadow — mirror traffic to the new model, compare offline, users&#10;   see nothing. BEST for model swaps (no user risk).&#10;A/B test — split by user cohort, measure CSAT/task completion.&#10;   Use when quality difference is subtle.&#10;&#10;LLM extra: per-SESSION stickiness (mid-conversation model swaps&#10;confuse users + break prompt-cache economics).&#10;This build&#39;s pattern: assistant-pro shipped NEXT TO the old&#10;assistant = a blue/green at feature level (zero-risk)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="460" y="60" width="400" height="310" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p12_hadr" value="HA / DR (the phi-dr pattern applied to an AI stack)&#10;&#10;Topology: ACTIVE zone + WARM standby zone behind a stable&#10;endpoint; LB health-check (2 fails ≈ 10s) steers ALL traffic to&#10;warm pods; HPA scales them to real load. RTO &lt; 30s, URL unchanged.&#10;&#10;AI-specific state map:&#10;• App/orchestrator tier — stateless → trivially replicated&#10;• Checkpoint DB + SQL — regional HA / replicas (RPO ≈ 0)&#10;• Vector DB — Qdrant replication or rebuild-from-source (vectors&#10;   are DERIVED data — re-embedding is the ultimate DR)&#10;• Model weights — local: bake into image/volume; cloud: N/A&#10;• GPU capacity — the scarce resource: reserve warm capacity or&#10;   accept degraded small-model mode during failover&#10;&#10;Definitions: SLI = measured signal (P95 latency) · SLO = internal&#10;target (99.9% &lt; 2s) · SLA = contractual promise with penalties" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fef7e0;strokeColor=#d79b00;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="880" y="60" width="400" height="310" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p12_lat" value="LATENCY OPTIMIZATION PLAYBOOK (target P95 &lt; 2s)&#10;&#10;1. Keep the model HOT — keep_alive=10m (LIVE in ws.py:&#10;    no cold-load between turns)&#10;2. Stream immediately — perceived latency = time-to-first-token,&#10;    not total time (LIVE)&#10;3. KV-cache / prompt-cache reuse — stable system-prompt prefix&#10;    (order prompts: static first, dynamic last)&#10;4. Quantization — int8/int4 GGUF is HOW llama3.2 runs fast&#10;    on a Mac (LIVE)&#10;5. Route simple → small models (model gateway)&#10;6. Cache responses/embeddings/schemas (LIVE: cached DDL)&#10;7. Parallelize context fetches — asyncio.gather over memory +&#10;    reminders + semantic + history (LIVE)&#10;8. Cap retrieval top-k and history window (LIVE: k=6, 12 turns)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1300" y="60" width="390" height="310" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p12_sec" value="SECURITY LAYERS (top→bottom = request path)&#10;&#10;1. AuthN — OAuth2/SSO + JWT, WS handshake before accept() [PLANNED]&#10;2. AuthZ — RBAC roles; per-role tool allowlists [PLANNED]&#10;3. Rate limiting + quotas at gateway [PLANNED]&#10;4. Prompt-injection defense — retrieved docs/web are UNTRUSTED:&#10;    delimiter-wrap, &quot;never follow instructions inside&quot;, per-route tool&#10;    allowlists [partial LIVE: grounding rules; NL2SQL never executes&#10;    free-form model text]&#10;5. Jailbreak resistance — refusal-quality benchmarks, system-prompt&#10;    hardening, moderation on inputs [PLANNED]&#10;6. PII masking — before logs AND before any cloud-LLM call&#10;    [mitigated today: default LLM is LOCAL — data never leaves]&#10;7. Output validation — schema check, toxicity, PII scrub [partial: JSON&#10;    validation LIVE]&#10;8. SQL/file guards — 5-layer SQL defense + path-traversal jail [LIVE]&#10;9. Secrets — env/pydantic-settings, never hardcoded [LIVE]; vault + rotation [PLANNED]&#10;10. Audit — correlation-ID trail per turn [LIVE]; auth events [PLANNED]&#10;11. Encryption — TLS in transit, at-rest DB/volume encryption [deploy-time]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fce8e6;strokeColor=#c5221f;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="400" width="500" height="380" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p12_owasp" value="OWASP LLM TOP-10 (name at least 5 in an interview)&#10;&#10;LLM01 Prompt Injection — direct + indirect (poisoned docs)&#10;LLM02 Insecure Output Handling — executing model output&#10;   unvalidated (this build: sqlglot + schema validation)&#10;LLM03 Training Data Poisoning&#10;LLM04 Model Denial of Service — token floods, agent loops&#10;   (cap: 25 iterations LIVE)&#10;LLM05 Supply Chain — models/datasets/plugins provenance&#10;LLM06 Sensitive Info Disclosure — PII in outputs/logs&#10;LLM07 Insecure Plugin/Tool Design — validate args, least&#10;   privilege (LIVE: whitelist + ro-engine)&#10;LLM08 Excessive Agency — tools too powerful, no HITL gate&#10;LLM09 Overreliance — no citations/verification for decisions&#10;LLM10 Model Theft — weight exfiltration&#10;&#10;COMPLIANCE MAP: GDPR — data locality (local-first ✓), right-to-&#10;erasure (delete by doc_id/entry ✓), consent, DPA · SOC2 — audit&#10;trails, access control, change mgmt · HIPAA — PHI isolation, BAA,&#10;encryption, minimum-necessary access" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fce8e6;strokeColor=#c5221f;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="560" y="400" width="440" height="380" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p12_resp" value="RESPONSIBLE AI + HITL&#10;&#10;• Bias — benchmark across demographics/languages; diverse eval sets&#10;• Toxicity — input+output moderation thresholds&#10;• Refusal quality — refuse the right things, not everything&#10;• Explainability — citations + shown SQL + route badges (LIVE) =&#10;   &quot;why did it answer this?&quot; is always answerable&#10;• Human-in-the-loop — low-confidence or high-risk answers route to&#10;   human review before delivery (queue + approve/edit/reject);&#10;   mandatory in healthcare/banking&#10;• Governance — model cards, decision log, incident runbook, review&#10;   board for new use-cases&#10;&#10;COST GOVERNANCE&#10;Per-user token quotas · daily budget alerts · cost per request on the&#10;dashboard · anomaly detection (runaway agent = cost spike) —&#10;foundation LIVE: token_usage table records provider/model/op/cost" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1020" y="400" width="330" height="380" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p12_drift" value="MONITORING &amp; DRIFT&#10;&#10;Watch: latency P95/P99 · error rate · token cost/day ·&#10;hallucination sampling · routing accuracy · feedback ratio&#10;&#10;Drift types:&#10;• Prompt drift — score trend per prompt version&#10;• Data drift — query-topic distribution shifts&#10;• Model drift — cloud provider silently updates the model&#10;   (pin versions; re-run evals on release notes)&#10;• Embedding drift — centroid distance on collections&#10;• Agent-loop runaway — iteration count + cost alarms&#10;   (cap LIVE: 25)&#10;&#10;Alert → triage → add to dataset → fix → canary → close.&#10;&#10;ROLLBACK: config-level revert (model/prompt version) &lt; 5 min,&#10;no deploy needed (LIVE pattern: DEFAULT_AI_MODEL +&#10;AgentPrompt.version); code-level = previous image." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1370" y="400" width="320" height="380" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p12_mgr" value="WHAT AN AI MANAGER ADDS BEYOND THE ENGINEERING (close the interview with this)&#10;&#10;Cost per request &amp; GPU utilization targets · SLA/SLO definitions and error budgets · rollout strategy choice + rollback drills · compliance sign-offs before GA · disaster-recovery runbook &amp; RTO/RPO commitments · feedback collection + human review workflows · governance (model cards, use-case review board) · vendor lock-in mitigation (provider abstraction — LIVE here) · team topology &amp; on-call · roadmap sequencing (value first, hardening before scale)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="810" width="1650" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

  <diagram id="p13" name="13 · Whiteboard — Transformer &amp; LLM Internals">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1240" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="p13_t" value="WHITEBOARD — TRANSFORMER &amp; LLM INTERNALS. &quot;Can you explain how ChatGPT works internally?&quot; — answer from first principles, then connect to the application layer (this platform)." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p13_evo" value="EVOLUTION OF NLP (30-second opener)&#10;&#10;Rules → classic ML → RNN → LSTM → GRU →&#10;TRANSFORMER (2017, &quot;Attention Is All You Need&quot;) →&#10;BERT / GPT → ChatGPT (RLHF) → AI Agents&#10;&#10;Why RNN/LSTM failed: &quot;The movie I watched last week&#10;was amazing because IT had a great story&quot; — by the time&#10;the model reaches &quot;it&quot;, sequential nets have forgotten&#10;&quot;movie&quot;. Long-context loss + sequential (no GPU&#10;parallelism) + slow training.&#10;&#10;Transformer&#39;s fix: look at EVERY word simultaneously&#10;(attention) → parallel training → scale → GPT." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="60" width="380" height="260" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p13_c1" value="Input text" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="470" y="60" width="200" height="34" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_c2" value="Tokenizer&#10;&quot;Hello everyone&quot; → [Hello][every][one] · BPE (GPT) / SentencePiece (Llama) · vocab ≈ 100-200k" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="450" y="122" width="240" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_c3" value="Embedding&#10;token → vector [0.32, 0.51, −0.14 … 768+ dims]; similar meanings sit close (king≈queen, car≈automobile)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="450" y="212" width="240" height="62" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_c4" value="Positional Encoding&#10;attention has no order sense — without it &quot;Dog bites man&quot; = &quot;Man bites dog&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="450" y="302" width="240" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_c5" value="N × Transformer layer&#10;Self-Attention → residual + LayerNorm → Feed-Forward → residual + LayerNorm" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="450" y="386" width="240" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_c6" value="Output layer&#10;probability over vocab → pick next token" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="450" y="474" width="240" height="50" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_c7" value="Next token → append → repeat&#10;decoder-only, AUTOREGRESSIVE — one token at a time (why streaming exists!)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="450" y="552" width="240" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_ce1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p13_c1" target="p13_c2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_ce2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p13_c2" target="p13_c3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_ce3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p13_c3" target="p13_c4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_ce4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p13_c4" target="p13_c5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_ce5" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p13_c5" target="p13_c6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_ce6" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p13_c6" target="p13_c7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_ce7" value="loop until stop token" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p13_c7" target="p13_c5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="730" y="490"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p13_attn" value="SELF-ATTENTION — the heart of GPT&#10;&#10;&quot;The animal didn&#39;t cross the street because IT was tired.&quot;&#10;What is &quot;it&quot;? The model ATTENDS to &quot;animal&quot; (not &quot;street&quot;) —&#10;relationships learned automatically.&#10;&#10;QKV — the Google-search analogy:&#10;Query (what I&#39;m looking for) → compare with Keys (what each&#10;token offers) → retrieve Values (the content). &quot;Capital of&#10;India&quot; → Q matches K=&quot;capital-city info&quot; → V=&quot;Delhi&quot;.&#10;&#10;Formula (explain, don&#39;t derive):&#10;Attention(Q,K,V) = softmax(QKᵀ / √dk) · V&#10;• Q·Kᵀ = relevance score between tokens&#10;• ÷ √dk = numerical stability&#10;• softmax = scores → probabilities&#10;• · V = weighted mix = contextual representation&#10;&#10;MULTI-HEAD: one head is one &quot;view&quot;; 32-64+ heads learn&#10;grammar, coreference (&quot;she&quot;→Mary), semantics in parallel.&#10;&#10;FFN + RESIDUALS + LAYERNORM: per-token nonlinear&#10;transform; residuals fix vanishing gradients (deep nets&#10;trainable); LayerNorm stabilizes training." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="740" y="60" width="440" height="440" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p13_adv" value="ADVANCED CONCEPTS (senior-level differentiators)&#10;&#10;KV CACHE — during generation, keys/values of past tokens are cached&#10;so each new token only computes attention against the cache. Why long&#10;chats slow down (cache grows) + why prompt caching is billed cheaper&#10;(reused prefix = reused KV). App-layer echo: keep_alive=10m (LIVE).&#10;&#10;MIXTURE OF EXPERTS — router activates 2-of-N expert FFNs per token:&#10;big capacity, small per-token compute (Mixtral-class economics).&#10;&#10;QUANTIZATION — weights fp16 → int8/int4 (GGUF): 4-8× smaller,&#10;faster, small quality loss. This is literally HOW llama3.2 runs on&#10;this Mac (LIVE via Ollama).&#10;&#10;SPECULATIVE DECODING — small draft model proposes tokens, big&#10;model verifies in one pass → 2-3× faster, identical output.&#10;&#10;CONTEXT WINDOW — attention is O(n²): window limits are compute&#10;limits. App answer: trim + summarize + RETRIEVE instead of carry.&#10;&#10;CHAIN OF THOUGHT — &quot;think step by step&quot; → intermediate reasoning&#10;tokens; reasoning models bake this in at RL time." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1200" y="60" width="490" height="440" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p13_train" value="TRAINING FAMILY — what each stage adds&#10;&#10;PRETRAINING — next-token prediction on trillions of tokens → raw capability&#10;SFT (Supervised Fine-Tuning) — instruction/answer pairs → follows instructions&#10;RLHF — humans rank outputs → reward model → PPO → helpful/harmless behavior&#10;   (the step that made GPT into ChatGPT)&#10;DPO — direct preference optimization: RLHF&#39;s effect without a reward model (simpler)&#10;DISTILLATION — big teacher trains small student → 3B models punch above weight&#10;   (why llama3.2-3B is usable at all)&#10;&#10;Why GPT feels intelligent = scale + attention + RLHF + instruction tuning&#10;+ APPLICATION LAYER: tools, RAG, memory, agents — pages 3-9 of this atlas." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="340" width="380" height="270" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p13_faq" value="INTERVIEW MICRO-ANSWERS&#10;&#10;Why tokenize? Vocabulary becomes manageable — ~100-200k learned&#10;tokens instead of millions of words; subwords handle unseen words&#10;(InsuranceClaimProcessing → Insurance·Claim·Process·ing).&#10;&#10;Token vs embedding? Token = text unit (ID). Embedding = its numeric&#10;vector representation carrying meaning.&#10;&#10;Why positional encoding? Attention is order-blind; positions make&#10;&quot;dog bites man&quot; ≠ &quot;man bites dog&quot;.&#10;&#10;Encoder vs decoder? BERT = encoder (understanding, bidirectional).&#10;GPT = decoder-only (generation, causal). T5 = both.&#10;&#10;&quot;HOW DOES CHATGPT ANSWER?&quot; — the 8-step script:&#10;1 prompt → 2 tokenized → 3 embeddings → 4 positional encoding →&#10;5 N× (self-attention + FFN) → 6 decoder predicts next token repeatedly →&#10;7 tokens → text → 8 application layer adds tools/RAG/memory/agents&#10;before the final response. (Step 8 = your differentiator: point at Page 3.)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="450" y="640" width="730" height="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13_conn" value="CONNECT INTERNALS → ARCHITECTURE (the senior move)&#10;&#10;Autoregressive decoding → why we STREAM tokens (Page 3)&#10;KV cache → why prompt PREFIX order matters + prompt caching economics&#10;Context O(n²) → why RAG retrieval beats stuffing history (Pages 5-6)&#10;Quantization → why local llama3.2 is feasible → privacy-first default (Page 10)&#10;Stateless model → why MEMORY is an app-layer service (Page 5)&#10;Hallucination = next-token guessing → why grounding + citations (Page 6)&#10;Instruction tuning limits → why guardrails validate OUTPUT (Pages 7, 12)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1200" y="640" width="490" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

  <diagram id="p14" name="14 · Interview Playbook">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1240" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="p14_t" value="INTERVIEW PLAYBOOK — the scripts, orders, numbers and trade-offs to rehearse. Everything here is backed by a page of this atlas + the live build at /assistant-pro." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p14_order" value="THE DESIGN-ANSWER ORDER (never deviate)&#10;&#10;Requirements → Architecture → Request Flow →&#10;LLM → RAG → Agents → Evaluation →&#10;Monitoring → Deployment&#10;&#10;30-SECOND SKELETON — &quot;Design ChatGPT from scratch&quot;:&#10;&quot;First functional + non-functional requirements — latency&#10;&lt;2s P95, 99.99%, compliance. Then the architecture: gateway&#10;→ auth → AI orchestrator with conversation, memory and&#10;prompt services → intent router → RAG / NL2SQL / agents /&#10;direct LLM → multi-provider model gateway with caching →&#10;streaming. Every response is traced, evaluated (RAGAS/&#10;golden set), and rated by users; feedback feeds the eval&#10;dataset. Deploy on K8s with canary + rollback; monitor&#10;latency, cost, hallucination, drift. I&#39;ve built exactly this&#10;shape — happy to go deep on any box.&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="60" width="400" height="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p14_scripts" value="SCRIPTED ANSWERS (rehearse verbatim, then personalize)&#10;&#10;&quot;WHY MODEL X?&quot; → the benchmark script (Page 10): shortlist by requirements →&#10;own-data eval set → 11 categories → weighted scorecard → &quot;best balance for OUR&#10;requirements&quot; + re-benchmark loop.&#10;&#10;&quot;HOW DO YOU EVALUATE AN LLM APP?&quot; → layered: (1) deterministic CI tests for&#10;guardrails/routing, (2) golden-dataset offline evals per release (RAGAS: faithfulness,&#10;context precision/recall; DeepEval rubrics), (3) online sampling + tracing with&#10;correlation IDs, (4) human feedback loop feeding the dataset, (5) business KPIs.&#10;Name the biases of LLM-as-judge (position, verbosity, self-preference) → instant depth.&#10;&#10;&quot;HOW DO YOU STOP HALLUCINATIONS?&quot; → prevention: route to grounded paths (RAG/&#10;SQL), low temperature, grounding prompts; detection: citations tied to real chunks,&#10;faithfulness evals, critic verification; containment: honesty fallback (&quot;not in your&#10;documents&quot;), HITL for high-risk; measurement: &lt;2% target, feedback loop.&#10;&#10;&quot;HOW DOES CHATGPT WORK?&quot; → 8-step script on Page 13, end with the application&#10;layer (that&#39;s where you live).&#10;&#10;&quot;WHAT WOULD YOU DO FIRST AS AI MANAGER?&quot; → discovery: use-cases + ROI + data&#10;audit (Page 2) → one thin end-to-end slice with evals → iterate. Value first, platform second." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="460" y="60" width="700" height="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p14_num" value="NUMBERS TO MEMORIZE&#10;&#10;$/M tokens (order-of-magnitude tiers):&#10;frontier ≈ $10-20 · mid ≈ $3-7 · small ≈ $0.1-1 ·&#10;local = $0 marginal (hardware amortized)&#10;&#10;Context windows: 8k · 32k · 128k · 200k · 1-2M&#10;&#10;Token math: 1 token ≈ ¾ word · 3k tokens/req ×&#10;500k req/day × $5/M ≈ $7.5k/day&#10;&#10;Capacity: 50k users ≈ 6 QPS avg, 60 peak ·&#10;GPU ≈ 1-3k tokens/s (7-13B batched)&#10;&#10;KPI targets: P95 &lt; 2s · hallucination &lt; 2% ·&#10;tool &gt; 98% · SQL &gt; 97% · JSON &gt; 99% ·&#10;cost &lt; $0.02/req · CSAT &gt; 4.6/5&#10;&#10;HA: RTO &lt; 30s zone failover · RPO ≈ 0 (regional HA DB)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1180" y="60" width="510" height="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p14_trade" value="TRADE-OFF FLASHCARDS (both sides + a verdict)&#10;&#10;RAG vs FINE-TUNING — RAG: fresh data, citations, no training, per-doc deletes&#10;(GDPR). FT: style/format/domain-language, latency (shorter prompts), but stale +&#10;no provenance + retrain cycle. Verdict: RAG for knowledge, FT for behavior; often both.&#10;&#10;LOCAL vs CLOUD LLM — Local: privacy, $0 marginal, no rate limits, offline; weaker&#10;ceiling, you own ops. Cloud: frontier quality, zero ops; data leaves, $, lock-in.&#10;Verdict: local default + cloud failover (this build) or cloud with PII masking.&#10;&#10;ONE BIG MODEL vs ROUTER + SMALL MODELS — Big: simpler, best quality everywhere,&#10;expensive. Router: 10× cheaper + faster on easy queries, needs routing accuracy&#10;monitoring. Verdict: router once volume &gt; ~10k req/day.&#10;&#10;BUY vs BUILD — Page 2 matrix. Verdict: buy the model, build orchestration + eval.&#10;&#10;LATENCY vs QUALITY — stream early, route hard queries to big models, cache;&#10;never make every user pay the frontier-model tax for &quot;hi&quot;.&#10;&#10;AGENT vs WORKFLOW — deterministic steps → workflow (cheaper, auditable);&#10;open-ended goals → agent loop with iteration caps + cost alarms." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="410" width="700" height="360" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p14_star" value="LEADERSHIP &amp; BEHAVIORAL (STAR skeletons)&#10;&#10;HALLUCINATION INCIDENT IN PROD — S: assistant invented a policy clause.&#10;T: contain + prevent recurrence. A: pulled route to HITL, added the case to the&#10;golden set, tightened grounding prompt + citation verification, canaried the fix.&#10;R: hallucination rate 3.1%→0.8%, incident runbook now standard.&#10;&#10;COST OVERRUN — S: token bill 3× forecast. T: cut cost without quality loss.&#10;A: token audit by route → cached FAQ answers, routed simple queries to small&#10;model, trimmed context, per-user quotas. R: −62% cost, quality KPIs flat.&#10;&#10;STAKEHOLDER CONFLICT (build vs buy) — S: leadership wanted vendor suite,&#10;eng wanted build. A: ran the weighted matrix + 4-week PoC on our data; presented&#10;TCO + differentiation. R: hybrid — bought model API, built orchestration; both&#10;sides owned the decision.&#10;&#10;FAILED PILOT — S: adoption 8%. A: user interviews → latency + trust issues →&#10;added streaming + citations + feedback button; re-piloted. R: 61% weekly active.&#10;Lesson: trust features (citations!) drive adoption more than raw accuracy.&#10;&#10;JUSTIFYING MODEL CHOICE TO LEADERSHIP — one slide: scorecard + cost&#10;curve + risk register + exit strategy (provider abstraction = no lock-in)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="760" y="410" width="640" height="360" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p14_red" value="RED FLAGS TO AVOID&#10;&#10;✗ &quot;We picked GPT because it&#39;s the best&quot;&#10;✗ User → LLM → Response as the whole design&#10;✗ No evaluation story (&quot;we eyeballed it&quot;)&#10;✗ No cost awareness (&quot;tokens are cheap&quot;)&#10;✗ Agents without iteration caps / cost alarms&#10;✗ Executing model output without validation&#10;✗ &quot;Fine-tune to add knowledge&quot; (that&#39;s RAG&#39;s job)&#10;✗ Ignoring prompt injection for RAG systems&#10;✗ No rollback plan for model/prompt changes" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fce8e6;strokeColor=#c5221f;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1420" y="410" width="270" height="250" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p14_wb" value="WHITEBOARD TIPS&#10;&#10;• Draw the spine first (user→gateway→orchestrator→&#10;   router→branches→LLM→response), THEN zoom&#10;• Say trade-offs out loud while drawing&#10;• Anchor claims: &quot;in my build, X worked like…&quot;&#10;• Ask 2 clarifying questions before drawing&#10;   (users? latency? data sensitivity?)&#10;• End every answer with eval + rollback —&#10;   that&#39;s what makes it &quot;senior&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1420" y="680" width="270" height="230" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
